; Copy this file to HAL9K.INI next to HAL9K.EXE and fill in where signups
; should go. HAL9K.INI is git-ignored: a webhook URL is a credential, so keep
; it out of the repository and out of screenshots.
;
; Nothing is sent unless this file exists, an address is filled in, and the
; signup is confirmed in the confirmation prompt.

; The signup service deployed from drillpress is preferred. It checks the
; fields, delivers the signup to hal9k and answers with a receipt.
[signup]
url=https://signup.hal9k.dk/api/signup

; A Slack incoming webhook can be used instead, for example when no signup
; service is reachable. The [signup] section wins when both are filled in.
;[slack]
;url=https://hooks.slack.com/services/REPLACE/ME/WITH_YOUR_WEBHOOK
